WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.580
2009.

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.480
AI hasn't taken off yet.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.703
Jensen Huang's message

00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:05.740
at Stanford:

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.455
don't just listen to customers.

00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:09.020
Listen to Moore's Law.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:09.792
Moore's Law:

00:00:09.812 --> 00:00:11.107
the number of transistors

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:11.581
on a chip

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.480
doubles about every two years.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.619
Most companies used it

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.150
to forecast technology.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:16.880
Jensen used it

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.450
to forecast the future.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.030
The 1990s.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:20.915
Gamers just wanted

00:00:20.935 --> 00:00:22.070
prettier graphics.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.075
NVIDIA built GPUs

00:00:23.095 --> 00:00:24.080
far more powerful

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.670
than anyone asked for.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.510
Customers said it cost too much.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:28.800
Jensen saw it differently:

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.492
Give the world

00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:30.629
enough computing power,

00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:32.630
and new applications will appear.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.300
He bet on the GPU.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.180
Then CUDA.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.240
Then AI.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.434
Fifteen years later,

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:39.285
the world is racing to build AI

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.610
on NVIDIA chips.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.190
Jensen's big lesson:

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:42.780
Customers talk

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.770
about the present.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.483
Technology talks

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:45.520
about the future.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.270
Great companies

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.790
don't just predict demand.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.125
They predict where technology

00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:49.790
takes us next.
